// Scenarios with the same When are checked against each other as one rule, when(a): (Given₁ ⇒ Then₁) ∧ (Given₂ ⇒ Then₂):
// where their Givens can hold together, with the specifications, both scenarios apply, so their Thens must hold
// together after the When. An input without a value (… with inputs job) is whatever the user inputs, so it can be any value.
// Expected: an error for 'Rush job' and 'Fast job': both apply to a busy printer (busy means a speed larger than 5),
//           but one Then sets the speed to 10 and the other to 3;
//           an error for 'Submit' and 'Resubmit': the same Given and the same input (whatever the user inputs), but
//           one Then adds it to the jobs and the other removes it;
//           an error for 'Submit' and 'Submit draft': when the user inputs "draft", both apply, but one Then adds it
//           to the jobs and the other removes it;
//           an error for 'Take job' and 'Drop job': both Thens dequeue the waiting as a variable, so the two are
//           aligned (job = next), but one Then adds it to the jobs and the other removes it;
//           no error for 'Slow job': its Given cannot hold together with the Given of 'Rush job' or 'Fast job';
//           no error for 'Resubmit' and 'Submit draft': both Thens remove the input from the jobs.

Entity Printer {
    Actions: print
    Data properties: speed: int, jobs: a list of string, waiting: a queue of string
    States: busy
}

Role Operator.

Action print { Initiators: Operator }
Action submit { Initiators: Operator, Input: job: string }
Action take { Initiators: Operator }

Declarative specification Printer is busy means {
    the speed larger than 5
}

Scenario: Rush job
Given the Printer is busy
When print is executed
Then the Printer's speed is set to 10.

Scenario: Fast job
Given the Printer's speed larger than 3
When print is executed
Then the Printer's speed is set to 3.

Scenario: Slow job
Given the Printer's speed smaller than 2
When print is executed
Then the Printer's speed is set to 1.

Scenario: Submit
Given submit is available
When submit is executed with inputs job
Then job is added to the Printer's jobs.

Scenario: Resubmit
Given submit is available
When submit is executed with inputs job
Then the Printer's jobs is removed with job.

Scenario: Submit draft
Given submit is available
When submit is executed with inputs job = "draft"
Then "draft" is removed from the Printer's jobs.

Scenario: Take job
Given take is available
When take is executed
Then the Printer's waiting is dequeued as job AND job is added to the Printer's jobs.

Scenario: Drop job
Given take is available
When take is executed
Then the Printer's waiting is dequeued as next AND the Printer's jobs is removed with next.
